   "text": "This SMILES is my reading of the drawing, with all residues assumed L-configured. The stereo was checked against the drawing only for the Glu in the left lipid chain and for the Pen2 alpha carbon. The other centres are inferred, not verified.\n\n**Peptide backbone.** I read it as Ac-Pen-Asn-Thr-Trp(7-Me)-Lys-Pen-Tyr(OCH2CH2NH2)-2Nal-Thp-Lys-Asn-3Pal-Sar-NH2:\n- The two Pen (penicillamine) residues are joined through an S\u2013S bond, which closes the macrocycle. Pen1 carries the N-acetyl group.\n- The Trp is 7-methylindol-3-yl.\n- The Tyr has a 2-aminoethyl ether on its phenol oxygen.\n- 2Nal is 2-naphthylalanine.\n- Thp is 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid.\n- 3Pal is 3-pyridylalanine.\n- The C-terminus is N-methylglycinamide (sarcosine amide).\n\n**Lipid side chains.** Both lysine side chains (the macrocycle Lys and the later Lys) carry the same substituent: two 8-amino-3,6-dioxaoctanoyl (AEEA) linkers, then \u03b3-Glu, then an N-acyl chain. I counted 14 carbons in the acyl chain on the left, giving tetradecanoyl. The right chain I assumed identical by symmetry, since I could not count its vertices reliably.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCC)C(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)SSC1(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(OCCN)cc1)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)C(=O)NC1(CCOCC1)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCC)C(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1cccnc1)C(=O)N(C)CC(N)=O"
